#: ../../../vba.md:37
msgid ""
"You can then attach `HelloWorld` to a button or run it directly in the VBA "
"Editor by hitting `F5`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../vba.md:40
msgid ""
"Place `xw.Book.caller()` within the function that is being called from Excel "
"and not outside as global variable. Otherwise it prevents Excel from "
"shutting down properly upon exiting and leaves you with a zombie process "
"when you use `Use UDF Server = True`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../vba.md:45
msgid "Function Arguments and Return Values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../vba.md:47
msgid ""
"While it's technically possible to include arguments in the function call "
"within `RunPython`, it's not very convenient. Also, `RunPython` does not "
"allow you to return values. To overcome these issues, use UDFs, see [User "
"Defined Functions (UDFs)](udfs.md#user-defined-functions-udfs) - however, "
"this is currently limited to Windows only."
msgstr ""
